  "answer": "The Atlas Logistics pilot was highly successful, with all measured results exceeding their targets [NL-020#NL-020-S04]. The quantified results were: 87.5% Weekly Active Usage (target >75%), 84.2% Query Success Rate (target >80%), 88.6% Citation Accuracy (target >85%), 4.8-week Median Onboarding Duration (target 5.0 weeks), 18.4% Support Escalation Decline (target >15%), and 1.8-second Average Query Latency (target <2.0) [NL-020#NL-020-S04].\n\nThe lessons drawn from the pilot recommend making pre-ingestion document cleanup mandatory, keeping permissions simple with broad department-level workspaces, and prioritizing mobile-friendly UI and messaging integrations for frontline staff [NL-020#NL-020-S07]. A standard 5-step onboarding checklist (ingestion queue audit, permissions mapping, frontline hardware check, supervisor webinars, and custom CSAT feedback loops) was also defined [NL-020#NL-020-S07].\n\nBased on this performance, the expansion recommendation is a phased, full company-wide rollout [NL-020#NL-020-S08]. Phase 1 expands to 500 users across Chicago, Dallas, and Atlanta (Q3 2026); Phase 2 implements advanced OCR for legacy scans (August 2026); Phase 3 transitions to the Enterprise Plan (Q4 2026) if user count exceeds 2,000, with Teams integration; Phase 4 builds automated API data pipelines and query audit scripts (Q1 2027) [NL-020#NL-020-S08].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
